\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Before Thy throne, O God, we kneel;
\par Give us a conscience quick to feel,
\par A ready mind to understand
\par The meaning of Thy chastening hand;
\par Whate'er the pain and shame may be,
\par Bring us, O Father, nearer Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Search out our hearts and make us true,
\par Wishful to give to all their due;
\par From love of pleasure, lust of gold,
\par From sins which make the heart grow cold,
\par Wean us and train us with Thy rod;
\par Teach us to know our faults, O God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. For sins of heedless word and deed,
\par For pride ambitious to succeed;
\par For crafty trade and subtle snare
\par To catch the simple unaware;
\par For lives bereft of purpose high,
\par Forgive, forgive, O Lord, we cry.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Let the fierce fires, which burn and try,
\par Our inmost spirits purify:
\par Consume the ill; purge out the shame;
\par O God! be with us in the flame;
\par A new-born people may we rise,
\par More pure, more true, more nobly wise.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

